worked at FBF Loans. No specific dates are provided, but this role preceded his position at C2 Financial.\u000a\u000a- **Champion Power Equipment**\u000a  - **Role:** Not explicitly stated, but described as a previous employer in his professional background.\u000a  - **Tenure:** Exact dates not available, but this role preceded his work in the financial sector.\u000a\u000a- **Mergers and Acquisitions Integration**\u000a  - **Role:** Professional in mergers and acquisitions integration (post-college)\u000a  - **Tenure:** After completing his undergraduate degree, Bright worked in M&A integration. No specific company or dates are provided, but this experience is referenced in his Vanderbilt Business biography.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a#### 3. **Education, Degrees, and Credentials**\u000a\u000a- **Concordia University Irvine**\u000a  - **Degree:** Bachelor’s degree (specific field not disclosed)\u000a  - **Graduation:** No specific graduation date is provided, but Bright attended Concordia University Irvine.\u000a\u000a- **Vanderbilt University**\u000a  - **Program:** MBA (Master of Business Administration)\u000a  - **Graduation:** No specific graduation date is provided, but Bright is listed in the Vanderbilt Business alumni directory.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a#### 4. **Professional Achievements, Awards, and Recognition**\u000a\u000a- No specific awards, recognitions, or industry accolades are publicly documented for Dylan Bright as of December 2025.\u000a- His professional achievements are primarily reflected in his career progression from M&A integration to loan origination and his association with reputable companies like C2 Financial and FBF Loans.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a#### 5. **LinkedIn Activity, Posts, and Thought Leadership**\u000a\u000a- No publicly available LinkedIn profile or activity for Dylan Bright is found as of December 2025.\u000a- No posts, articles, or thought leadership content attributed to Bright on LinkedIn or other professional platforms